---
metadata:
  title: Find a space
---
{%- comment -%}
  Scaffold homepage. It exists to prove the module wiring works end to end:
  current_profile resolves, roles come back, can_do answers, and the module's
  own auth pages are reachable. The real homepage (hero over map, Free-to-List
  band, featured listings) gets ported once near_me_listings exists.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  function current_profile = 'modules/user/helpers/current_profile'
  function can_view_admin = 'modules/user/helpers/can_do', requester: current_profile, do: 'admin_pages.view', entity: null, access_callback: null
  function can_register = 'modules/user/helpers/can_do', requester: current_profile, do: 'users.register', entity: null, access_callback: null
  function modules_installed = 'modules/core/queries/registry/search', type: 'module'
-%}

<h1>Desks Near Me</h1>
<p class="muted">Module-first rebuild. This is scaffolding, not the real homepage.</p>

<h2>Auth state</h2>
<table class="pos-table">
  <tbody>
    <tr><th scope="row">Signed in</th><td>{% if context.current_user %}yes, {{ context.current_user.email }}{% else %}no{% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Profile id</th><td>{{ current_profile.id | default: '(none)' }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Roles</th><td>{{ current_profile.roles | join: ', ' | default: '(none)' }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">can_do admin_pages.view</th><td>{{ can_view_admin }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">can_do users.register</th><td>{{ can_register }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Installed modules</h2>
{%- comment -%}
  registry/search fires the module_info hook. None of the modules we installed
  ships a hook_module_info implementation, so this is empty, and the core
  module's claim that manifests register themselves does not hold. Versions are
  authoritative in pos-module.lock.json, not here.
{%- endcomment -%}
<ul>
  {%- for m in modules_installed -%}
    <li>{{ m.name | default: m.machine_name }} {{ m.version }}</li>
  {%- else -%}
    <li class="muted">Empty, as expected: no installed module implements hook_module_info. See pos-module.lock.json for pinned versions.</li>
  {%- endfor -%}
</ul>

<h2>Module endpoints</h2>
<ul>
  <li><a href="/users/new">/users/new</a> registration form</li>
  <li><a href="/sessions/new">/sessions/new</a> sign in</li>
  <li><a href="/passwords/reset">/passwords/reset</a> reset password</li>
</ul>
